F10: Depends on the selected detector. A perplexity-based heuristic check (LLMRails only) or an embedding classifier served by an NVIDIA model service. If the detector is unreachable, requests are let through. Several third-party guards also offer jailbreak or prompt-injection detection. [Documented]
F11: • Depends on the selected flow [Documented]
• Heuristics check length-per-perplexity (threshold 89.79) [Documented]
• Heuristics check prefix/suffix perplexity (threshold 1845.65, inputs over 20 words) [Documented]
• Both heuristic thresholds are configurable and must be above 0; the code defaults match the docs [Documented]
• Heuristics run in-process only with transformers and torch installed (perplexity uses gpt2-large); the manifest declares both as optional dependencies, and a server_endpoint avoids the local install [Documented]
• In-process mode is for testing only [Documented]
• Production should set server_endpoint [Documented]
• Model flow uses a random forest on Snowflake Arctic embeddings [Documented]
• Model flow is called through the NemoGuard JailbreakDetect NIM [Documented]
  – settings: nim_base_url, nim_server_endpoint (code default classify), and api_key (takes precedence) or api_key_env_var
  – the tutorial sets the endpoint to /v1/security/nvidia/nemoguard-jailbreak-detect
  – nim_url and nim_port are deprecated
• Engine support: heuristics run on LLMRails only (IORails blocks them because the backend is ambiguous, issue #2285) [Documented]
• Engine support: model flow runs on both engines [Documented]
• If the detector is unreachable the rail allows the request (fails open) [Documented]
• NIM training data: the model card says a combination of three open datasets, de-duplicated and reviewed, while the NVIDIA docs page names different datasets (AdvBench, ToxicChat, JailbreakChat and 1000 Dolly-15k examples), so the two sources disagree [Documented]
• Optional third-party backends (all-in-one guards whose NVIDIA pages state jailbreak/prompt-injection detection):
  – AutoAlign (autoalign check input; page lists a jailbreak detection guardrail, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/auto-align; runs on LLMRails and IORails) [Documented] (licensing to be verified) [To be verified]
  – Pangea AI Guard (pangea ai guard input; page lists prompt injection attacks, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/pangea; runs on LLMRails and IORails) (deprecated per NVIDIA third-party page) [Documented] (licensing to be verified) [To be verified]
  – CrowdStrike AIDR (crowdstrike aidr guard input; page lists prompt injection and jailbreak attempts, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/crowdstrike-aidr; runs on LLMRails and IORails) [Documented] (commercial vendor; subscription required, contact-sales) [Documented: vendor site]
  – Trend Micro (trend ai guard input; page lists prompt injection attacks, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/trend-micro; runs on LLMRails and IORails) [Documented] (commercial vendor; free trial and contact-sales, no public price; AI Guard product page not checked) [To be verified]
  – Fiddler (fiddler user safety; page says it detects jailbreaking inputs, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/fiddler; runs on LLMRails and IORails) [Documented] (paid / non-OSS service with free tier) [Documented: vendor site]
  – Guardrails AI (guardrailsai check input $validator=...; page lists jailbreak detection validators such as detect_jailbreak, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/guardrails-ai; runs on LLMRails and IORails) [Documented] (open-source, Apache-2.0) [Documented: vendor site]
  – HF classifier (hf classifier check input $classifier=prompt_injection; page shows prompt injection detection on the input rail, https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/guardrails/configure-guardrails/guardrail-catalog/third-party/hf-classifier; runs on LLMRails and IORails) [Documented] (licence depends on the chosen model) [To be verified]

